From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 23:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: start the sensor DSP

The motion sensors on this handset live behind the SLPI, a separate Hexagon
island, and nothing reaches them while it is held in reset. The node is already
described upstream with its SMP2P interrupts and memory region, and the board
already reserves the stock 0x98100000 window for it; only the firmware name and
status were missing.

The image comes from the handset's own modem partition, where the vendor ships
it as slpi.mdt plus twenty-two segments, squashed into a single slpi.mbn the way
the other remote processors here are packaged.

Signed-off-by: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -583,6 +583,11 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&remoteproc_slpi {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8150/oneplus/hotdog/slpi.mbn";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &remoteproc_mpss {
 	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8150/oneplus/hotdog/modem.mbn";
 	status = "okay";
--
2.50.1
